\description{
Test clusters (a cluster channel from explore) or populations between groups of samples defined by a metadata field, with pairing and covariates as fixed effects. test "state" (default) is diffcyt-DS-limma: per sample, the median of arcsinh(x / cofactor) of each marker in each cluster or population (cofactor 5 for mass cytometry, 150 for fluorescence), clusters with at least minCells cells in at least half the samples, a linear model per cluster and marker weighted by the cells in each sample, limma's moderated t-statistics with a mean-variance trend, and Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment across every cluster and marker tested. By default it tests the markers the clustering did not use (state markers). test "abundance" tests each cluster's share of the parent population with a quasi-binomial model. Rows are sorted by p; logFC is the difference of the medians (contrast minus reference).
